// --- ?fog: big light (21.10, after Drifter Star) ---
// Our sky was the same fine pattern at the same brightness all over (wallpaper); Drifter's is one or two big bright
// masses and dark gulfs, its billows drawn only where it is lit. So: a low-frequency field a screen or two across at a
// far depth (it moves with the camera by that depth, the parallax stays), the sky's own detail lifted in the light and
// dying in the shade, a soft glow of the mass itself.
//   1 the sky's own palette;  2 the same light in one hue against the hero's colour (the default, Artem 22.10): steel
//     blue round a warm hero, teal round a magenta one, a dark warm plum round the blue giant and a white hero, eased
//     over a transformation (space.ts fogPal), so the hero never sinks into its sky (?fogpal=0: always steel blue);
//   3 the cold fog at three depths (far masses, a nearer mass of its own, a thin veil drifting in front), the light of
//     each breathing slowly, a pulse running through it.
// The field is smooth, so it is worked out at 1/8 of the screen (fogField, space.ts's pass uPart 2, ~+11 ms at 8.3 MP
// done per pixel) and read back here bilinearly: r the far field, g the region of light, b the light the masses add,
// a the nearer mass (3).
